  <decisions>[{"id": "TD-2026-08-01-893", "decision": "stake recover seals an explicit reversion strand rather than silently moving the tip pointer", "rationale": "Closes C-4 and C-12 with one mechanism, preserves append-only and the linear v2 chain, works on the live v1/v2 fabric where the v3-DAG option would have removed disaster recovery entirely, and makes the rollback auditable — the git-parity answer, since git records a reset in the reflog."}, {"id": "MIGRATE-LIVE-FABRIC", "decision": "Ran `warpline refs migrate` on the live fabric, after a verified backup", "rationale": "The repo was in legacy selvage mode, which disengaged the pickId ref CAS and left only a stateId CAS blind to 11 of 64 strands. Combined with the installed backgrounded auto-seal hook, that was the one path to permanent corruption of real data. Migration touched no strands (ledger md5 unchanged) and downgrades a broken-mutex race from unrepairable corruption to a reported abandoned head."}]</decisions>
  <learnings>["The highest-value action in a remediation batch may be a command that already exists. `refs migrate` was advertised by the CLI's own output, closed the only live-data corruption path, and required no code. Check what the tool is already telling you before writing anything.", "When a fix breaks a legitimate tested behaviour, that collision is information, not an obstacle — it revealed that two separately-filed audit findings were one mechanism. An agent that reverts and documents beats one that forces the fix through or weakens the test.", "For discriminators, prefer a structural signal over parsing errors: `ls-tree` exits 0 with empty output for a genuine absence, whereas `git show` exits 128 for both absence and corruption. The exit code could not have carried the distinction, and a wrong discriminator there would have broken every add/delete merge.", "Track the SKIPPED count, not just the passing count. 744/5-skipped to 749/0-skipped is the real delta; a green suite that is green because tests are skipped reproduces the exact defect the audit was convened to fix.", "Fixes leave stale user-facing strings behind. Module docs got updated while `cli.ts` still described the old contract — and on a product whose F4 arc is about cold agents learning from runtime self-description, a description that contradicts its implementation is a teaching-surface defect, not a typo."]</learnings>
